{
 "format": "nte-guides",
 "format_version": 1,
 "_source": "https://www.prydwen.gg/neverness-to-everness/characters/<slug> - the Build tab, read on 2026-08-21 through a real browser session at their stated Crawl-delay of 10s.",
 "_priority_is_substats": "`priority` is Prydwen's Sub Stats ranking, which is what the field documents. Their separate Main Stats ranking is not merged in: combining two published rankings into one would be our construction, not theirs. A main-stat-only priority (usually the elemental DMG bonus) therefore keeps its published target but sits at weight 1.",
 "_ties": "Prydwen writes ties as `A = B` and emphasis as `>>`. Both are flattened to a plain ordering that keeps the printed left-to-right order, because the schema forbids duplicate ranks.",
 "_targets_omit_totals": "Prydwen's `HP:`, `ATK:` and `DEF:` endgame lines are character TOTALS. The vector the solver scores is gear + Arc only and carries no character base stats, so those three are not comparable and are left out rather than mapped to the flat gear slots, which would be a units error. Every other published line has a zero or negligible base component and is carried through as published. Note Crit DMG still includes the character's ~50% base, so that target is conservative rather than exact.",
 "_ranges": "Where a range or a conditional was published (`50% ~ 80%+`, `64-74%+`, `100%+ before 80% from Arc buff`) the lower bound is used, since a target is a floor to reach.",
 "_absent": "A character with no published build data is absent, not guessed: linko.",
 "_shape": {
  "key": "the GA_<key>_* ability key, so it joins to a capture directly",
  "sets": "Prydwen's ranked cartridge set recommendation. Recorded as published; the solver still enumerates every owned set itself.",
  "variants": "one per published priority set",
  "targets": "recommended endgame stats, raw stat ids, percentages as fractions",
  "priority": "substat ranking, best first; weights are derived from position",
  "updated": "the date this entry was read from Prydwen, not their revision date"
 },
